  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Food Inspector, Dept. Of Pfa, Govt. Of ... vs Kailash Chand on 31 August, 2015 Bench: Dipak Misra, R. Banumathi Crl.A.1138/15 1 In The Supreme Court Of India Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Appeal No.1138 Of 2015 (Arising out of S.L.P.(Crl.) No.10266 of 2014) Food Inspector, Department of Pfa Appell Govt. of Nct of Delhi Versus Shri Kailash Chand Respon O R D E R Leave granted. Heard Mr. Neeraj Kishan Kaul, learned Additional Solicitor General for the appellant and Mrs. K. Sarda Devi, learned counsel for the respondent.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "It is submitted by Mr. Neeraj Kishan Kaul, learned Additional Solicitor General that the High Court has not kept itself alive to two aspects, namely, the mandate of Section 13(3) of the PFA Act and the language employed in Rules 23, 28 and 29 of the 1955 Rules. Section 13(3) of the PFA Act reads as follows: The certificate issued by the Director of the Central Food Laboratory under sub-section (2B) shall supersede the report given by the public analyst under sub-section (1).",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is submitted by Mr. Neeraj Kishan Kaul, learned Additional Solicitor General that the High Court has not kept itself alive to two aspects, namely, the mandate of Section 13(3) of the PFA Act and the language employed in Rules 23, 28 and 29 of the 1955 Rules.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Section 13(3) of the PFA Act reads as follows: The certificate issued by the Director of the Central Food Laboratory under sub-section (2B) shall supersede the report given by the public analyst under sub-section (1)."
  },
